cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ECOCIDE: Pre-registered, exposure-based satellite analysis of the vegetation effects of the Kakhovka Dam destruction"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maske"
    given-names: "Sakshi D."
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/ECOCIDE"
url: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/ECOCIDE"
abstract: >-
  Code, analysis plans and results for a pre-registered, pixel-level test of
  the vegetation effects of the Kakhovka Dam destruction (6 June 2023) using
  MODIS NDVI (250 m, 2010-2024). Treatment is defined by exposure (flooded
  land, drained reservoir bed, canal-irrigated cropland) and comparisons are
  made inside the war zone, with a registered revision adding VIINA occupation
  and conflict data and annual water masks. Flooded land did not lose summer
  greenness (except floodplain wetlands); the relative decline of canal-zone
  farmland predates the invasion and did not deepen after the breach; about
  1,500 km2 of the former reservoir became vegetated by 2024. Study 1
  (Kherson Oblast vs Romanian counties, monthly Sentinel-2 NDVI) is retained.
  Zenodo v1.0.0 and EarthArXiv preprint v1 report an earlier, superseded
  analysis.
keywords:
  - pre-registration
  - MODIS
  - ecocide
  - remote sensing
  - causal inference
  - difference-in-differences
  - satellite evidence
  - Kakhovka Dam
  - NDVI
  - geospatial analysis
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21757974"
    description: "Zenodo archive of the earlier ECOCIDE v1.0.0 (superseded analysis); not this version"
